        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a cluster of `tui_app_server` regressions in startup, login, and shutdown behavior:\r\n\r\n- Fixes a fatal startup error when launching the CLI while logged out:\r\n  `account/rateLimits/read failed during TUI bootstrap`\r\n- Fixes terminal cleanup on early TUI exit paths, which could leave behind a stray `%` in `zsh`. This affects both tui and tui_app_server paths\r\n- Fixes ChatGPT login browser launch so the local browser opens again for in-process `tui_app_server` login flows\r\n- Fixes slow `Ctrl+C` exit from the \u201cFinish signing in with your browser\u201d screen by canceling the active login attempt before onboarding shutdown\r\n\r\n## Root Causes\r\n\r\n### Logged-out bootstrap failure\r\nDuring TUI bootstrap, `tui_app_server` fetched account rate limits unconditionally and treated any failure as fatal. When the user was logged out, the account bootstrap response had no ChatGPT account, so the rate-limit RPC failed and aborted startup.\r\n\r\n### Stray `%` after exit\r\nSeveral app-server TUI paths could return after `tui::init()` without guaranteeing terminal restore. That left the shell inheriting a dirty terminal state, which showed up as a highlighted `%` prompt marker in `zsh`.\r\n\r\n### ChatGPT browser not opening\r\nIn the app-server-backed login flow, the backend intentionally starts the ChatGPT login server with `open_browser: false`, but the TUI client never opened the returned `auth_url` itself. As a result, the browser never launched.\r\n\r\n### Slow `Ctrl+C` on login screen\r\n`Esc` canceled the active auth attempt, but onboarding-level `Ctrl+C` quit bypassed that cancellation path. The TUI exited while the login server was still running, and in-process app-server shutdown then waited on that stale login attempt.\r\n\r\n## Fixes\r\n\r\n- Rate-limit bootstrap is now gated so it only runs when OpenAI auth is required and a ChatGPT account is actually present; failures are treated as non-fatal and fall back to empty snapshots\r\n- Added guaranteed terminal restore guards around TUI startup/exit paths so fatal and early-return flows restore the terminal cleanly\r\n- The app-server TUI now opens ChatGPT `auth_url`s locally for in-process login flows, including the device-code fallback-to-browser path\r\n- Auth cancellation is now centralized and reused by both `Esc` and onboarding `Ctrl+C`\r\n- In-process app-server shutdown now explicitly drops any active ChatGPT login before draining background work\r\n",
